<h2 class=3D"wp-block-heading" id=3D"h-recipe-inspiration">Recipe Inspirati=
on</h2>



<p>This recipe draws inspiration from both French and Italian cuisines. <a =
href=3D"https://minimalistbaker.com/easy-ratatouille-versatile-1-pot/" targ=
et=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noreferrer noopener">Ratatouille</a> is a classic Fren=
ch dish with onion, garlic, tomato, zucchini, eggplant, bell pepper, and le=
afy herbs. </p><div id=3D"AdThrive_Content_1_desktop" class=3D"adthrive-ad =
 adthrive-content adthrive-content-1" style=3D"min-height: 250px;"></div>



<p>The Italian inspiration comes from the additions of <a href=3D"https://m=
inimalistbaker.com/italian-herb-crispy-baked-tofu/" target=3D"_blank" rel=
=3D"noreferrer noopener">Crispy Italian Herb Baked Tofu</a> and <a href=3D"=
https://minimalistbaker.com/creamy-pesto-sauce/" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"n=
oreferrer noopener">Creamy Pesto Sauce</a>. Neither dish is classically Ita=
lian=E2=80=94instead, they draw inspiration in terms of flavor and concept.=
</p>



<h2 class=3D"wp-block-heading" id=3D"h-how-to-make-sheet-pan-ratatouille">H=
ow to Make Sheet Pan Ratatouille</h2>



<p>While ratatouille is traditionally made on the stovetop, this recipe goe=
s in a different direction with the use of a sheet pan. Not only is it <str=
ong>quick, easy, and hands-off</strong>, but roasting the vegetables create=
s <strong>caramelized edges</strong> and enhances their sweetness.</p>



<p>For the vegetables, we use classic ratatouille ingredients including zuc=
chini, eggplant, onion, and bell pepper. They=E2=80=99re seasoned simply wi=
th salt, dried Italian herbs, and olive oil.</p><div id=3D"AdThrive_Content=
_2_desktop" class=3D"adthrive-ad  adthrive-content adthrive-content-2" styl=
e=3D"min-height: 250px;"></div>



