1" class=3D"wprm-recipe-instruction" style=3D"list-style-type: decimal;"><d=
iv class=3D"wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style=3D"margin-bottom: 5px;">To =
one baking sheet, add the zucchini, eggplant, red onion, and red bell peppe=
r. Add the salt, Italian herbs, and olive oil. Toss to evenly coat and spre=
ad the veggies so they=E2=80=99re overlapping as little as possible.</div><=
/li><li id=3D"wprm-recipe-120944-step-0-2" class=3D"wprm-recipe-instruction=
" style=3D"list-style-type: decimal;"><div class=3D"wprm-recipe-instruction=
-text" style=3D"margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style=3D"display: block;">Next, =
prepare the <a href=3D"https://minimalistbaker.com/italian-herb-crispy-bake=
d-tofu/" target=3D"_blank">Italian Herb Tofu</a>, adding it to the other pa=
rchment-lined baking sheet.</span></div></li><li id=3D"wprm-recipe-120944-s=
tep-0-3" class=3D"wprm-recipe-instruction" style=3D"list-style-type: decima=
l;"><div class=3D"wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style=3D"margin-bottom: 5px=
;"><span style=3D"display: block;">Place both baking sheets in the oven =E2=
=80=94 the vegetables on the upper rack and the tofu below =E2=80=94 and co=
ok for 15 minutes. After 15 minutes, flip the tofu with a spatula, then add=
 the cherry tomatoes on top of the roasted veggies and bake both for anothe=
r 15 minutes, or until the tofu is a little firm and golden with crispy edg=
es, the veggies are slightly caramelized, and the tomatoes are beginning to=
 burst.</span></div></li><li id=3D"wprm-recipe-120944-step-0-4" class=3D"wp=
rm-recipe-instruction" style=3D"list-style-type: decimal;"><div class=3D"wp=
rm-recipe-instruction-text" style=3D"margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style=3D"di=
splay: block;">While everything is in the oven, make your <a href=3D"https:=
//minimalistbaker.com/creamy-pesto-sauce/" target=3D"_blank">Creamy Pesto S=
auce</a> and prepare any pasta or polenta to serve with your ratatouille.</=
span></div></li><li id=3D"wprm-recipe-120944-step-0-5" class=3D"wprm-recipe=
-instruction" style=3D"list-style-type: decimal;"><div class=3D"wprm-recipe=
-instruction-text" style=3D"margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style=3D"display: bl=
ock;">Serve the ratatouille and tofu over your pasta, polenta, or grains, d=
rizzle with the creamy pesto sauce, and sprinkle with vegan parmesan cheese=
 (optional). Enjoy! Leftovers keep stored separately for 3-4 days in the re=
frigerator, or in the freezer for 1 month. Any leftover Creamy Pesto Sauce =
can be used on pasta, veggies, and beyond!</span></div></li></ul></div></di=
v>
